id: pm-ado-1udj
title: Consume the canonical pm-ops attestation gate rather than carrying a twentieth vendored copy
description: "This package was scaffolded from the fleet starter, which still carries the publish-attestation gate as vendored source: scripts/shell-command-scan.ts and scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts are copies, not launchers. Nineteen repositories already carry nineteen divergent versions of exactly these files, and the fleet is converging them onto canonical exports published by pm-ops so a bypass fixed once is fixed everywhere.\n\nScaffolding a new package from the starter therefore creates a twentieth copy the moment it is created. It must join the same convergence wave rather than be treated as a special case, and it cannot converge until pm-ops publishes the exports: the released pm-ops 2026.8.31 exports only the package root, docstrings and assurance, while shell-scan and attestation exist on an unmerged branch.\n\nThe docstring gate is already the shape to copy, since scripts/docstring-gate.ts is a thin launcher over the canonical pm-ops docstrings export."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:gates","area:supply-chain",de-vendor
created_at: "2026-09-02T18:06:25.457Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-02T18:06:25.892Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "Both scripts are thin launchers over the published pm-ops exports rather than copies; a test fails if the gate is a local copy rather than the resolved package export, so a later hand edit cannot re-fork the lineage"
risk: high
blocked_by: pm-ops must publish the shell-scan and attestation exports first
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/81",project,canonical exports plus the closed fail-opens
